**Done:** all GraphitiTarget source files (target.ts, isolation.ts, cypher.ts, namespace.ts, baseline.ts, pi-config/args/session/process.ts, artifact-reader.ts, probe.ts), the fake pi/Neo4j test infra, full test suite (namespace, pi-config, pi-args, pi-session, baseline, isolation, target, probe, real-smoke), infra/graphiti/docker-compose.yml, contracts/graphiti/mcp-config.yaml, scripts/graphiti-infra.sh, and the README — all verified via `pnpm typecheck` and `pnpm check` (375/375 TS tests + all shell tests green) before node broke. The grep isolation gate also passes.

**Remaining:** re-verify `pnpm check` once node is fixed, run the mutation-evidence edit/test/revert cycles, then commit. I'll continue as soon as the environment notification lands — no need to prompt me further in the meantime.
